userStories.description:
**Goal** — Make the workflow feature record store the advisor approval outcome (with decision id), the CI wait detail and the per-story states, so later stages can build a complete open-items list.

**Motivation** — The facts are lost before the verdict is built: `askApproval` returns `{ approved, rationale }` with no decision id; `publish` folds the rationale into `reasons` and drops the rest; the CI wait's `detail` text (the source of the conflicting, no-checks and unavailable reasons) is not stored; and the story states live in `result.stories` and in the run's story summaries, which `buildVerdict(record)` never sees.

**Approach**
- `askApproval` (`src/workflow/approval.ts:98`): Baseline `Promise<{ approved: boolean; rationale: string }>`. Target `Promise<ApprovalOutcome>`. `decisionId` is the returned `AdviceDecision.id`; it is absent (no key) when the advisor returned no decision or threw.
- The CI reason in `readinessReasons`: Baseline inline per-state ternaries. Target `export function ciReason(ci: FeatureCiState | undefined, detail?: string): string | undefined` in `approval.ts`, returning `CI failed` for `failed`, `detail ?? <the existing default>` for `conflicting` / `no-checks` / `unavailable`, and `undefined` for `green` / `pending` / `skipped` / `undefined`. `readinessReasons` calls it, so its output is unchanged. (The default for `conflicting` is `PR has merge conflicts with its base branch`.)
- `PublishOutcome` (`src/workflow/finalize.ts:37`): Baseline `{ outcome; ci; url?; reasons }`. Target adds `approval?: ApprovalOutcome` (present only when the advisor was asked) and `ciDetail?: string` (present only when `ci` is `conflicting`, `no-checks` or `unavailable`).
- `WorkflowFeatureRecord` (`src/workflow/types.ts:172`): adds `approval?: ApprovalOutcome`, `ciDetail?: string` and `storyStates?: readonly StoryStateItem[]`. All three are absent on records written before this feature.
- `publishStep` (`src/workflow/feature-machine.ts:453`): also returns `approval` and `ciDetail` when the outcome carries them, and `storyStates` built from `env.facts.stories` (`{ id, state, reason? }`, in that order).
- Test harness: `test/helpers/workflow-feature-machine.ts` publish step returns the fixed `PUBLISHED` outcome; add an optional `published?: PublishOutcome` script field that it returns instead when set (existing callers unchanged). `finalize-ci-gate.test.ts` `wire(ci)` gains an optional second argument `{ hold?: { id: string; rationale: string } }` that makes its advisor return a `hold` decision with that id and rationale; existing tests update: 'conflict keeps draft' now also carries `ciDetail: "PR has merge conflicts with main"`; approval.test askApproval expectations carry `decisionId` on decision paths (no-decision and throw cases carry none); finalize.test 'happy path' now also carries `approval: { approved: true, rationale, decisionId }`.

**Scope** — In: ApprovalOutcome/StoryStateItem types, askApproval, ciReason, PublishOutcome fields, publish wiring, publishStep record fields, test harness changes. Out: any change to buildOpenItems, OpenItem.kind, upsertFeatureRecord, finishPr/PrParts, and the NOTHING_VERIFIED/gateReasons/storyReasons exports (US-002) and the CLI command (US-003). Feature-level: BLOCKING_KINDS and approvalEvidence/finish-approval question are unchanged.

**Interface**
```typescript
// src/workflow/types.ts
export interface ApprovalOutcome { readonly approved: boolean; readonly rationale: string; readonly decisionId?: string }
export interface StoryStateItem { readonly id: string; readonly state: StoryState; readonly reason?: string }
// WorkflowFeatureRecord gains:
//   approval?: ApprovalOutcome; ciDetail?: string; storyStates?: readonly StoryStateItem[]
// src/workflow/approval.ts
export function askApproval(...): Promise<ApprovalOutcome>
export function ciReason(ci: FeatureCiState | undefined, detail?: string): string | undefined
// src/workflow/finalize.ts PublishOutcome gains: approval?: ApprovalOutcome; ciDetail?: string
```
